+## Work in a narrow window or with large text
+
+When the main toolbar changes to **Actions…** in a narrow window, open that menu to reach its original document, inspection and geometry actions. The wide window restores the normal toolbar buttons. Use the inspector’s vertical scrollbar to reach document controls and the **Solids**, **Mesh**, **Inspect**, **Organize** and **Publish** pages. If a page is wider than the inspector, use the horizontal scrollbar at its bottom to bring the left or right action column fully into view. Pressing Tab moves focus between controls and brings the focused control into view. Different scroll positions show different columns; controls need not all be visible at once. The native geometry view remains separate from the inspector, and scrolling the inspector does not change geometry, units or History.
+
+For source-grounded worked examples, extract the separate illustrated HTML guide and open its index. It covers generated inputs, exact solids, measurements, constraints, units, publication, face images, Recipe replay and document recovery.
